My first ever ASCENSION! Excuse the drippy enthusiasm, but I'm just going to 
take the opportunity to expatiate at length. I have a number of  
questions, but for the most part, I just want to exult in the details of 
this ASCENSION!

The game started off unremarkably. Being an archaeologist, my character
had no money problems. However, during a close fight with a troll, I zapped
myself with a wand of invisibility and effectively barred myself from any
further transactions with shopkeepers.

I found a long sword and was able to dip for Excalibur. In the meantime, 
I managed to acquire a resevoir of holy water. THEN, I found a pair of 
gauntlet of powers AND an amulet of life saving. I also had an AC of -22 
(courtesy of tremendous charity to
the (later killed) priest of Huehotol). With this gear, I was
invulnerable to anything Nethack could have thrown my way. I felt that
this game would be the one. I was going to ascend I thought, and no 
programmed monster or trap would stop me. 

And I was right. The biggest enemy turned out to be myself. I carelessly hit
Ctrl-Z and *poof* my game was suspended. Thus came a waiting period of two
weeks while the game and my character were sitting in total disuse. (BTW, I
really  think the Dev team should delete that key stroke from the UNIX
version. It was never on the pc version: imagine my surprise then, when 
this predicament suddendly springs on me. Game suspended I think, no problem.
husc8% nethack
Destroy old character?  [yn]
huhh? what happened? Oh SHIT!!! Where is the character? [Long train 
of expletives deleted]
anyway, Query1: What is the point of the Ctrl-Z keystroke? A malicious
trick for those notoriously bad typers? 
back to the story...)

My game eventually gets back on line. I traipse through the Gnomish Mines
and the Dugeons of Doom. I reach the castle and find a wand of wishing. Cool.
Wish for blessed rustproof +2 gray dragon scale mail, and pocket the final
wish for later use. Feeling especially confident, I send my character into
the Valley of Doom. Only to lose an  AoLS to a nalfshanee. Well, actually
to a Blue Dragon, Yellow Dragon, Green Dragon and Minotaur that  he summons.
I survive, but while dispatching the heavy shock troopers, a pesky gremlin
sneaks in and steals my protection attribute. AC drops to -13. No
problem I think: I'll just get it back from that neutral priest of Calaxi.
To my utter disappointment, I found that he would not give it back to me.
So, with my trusty wand of polymorph, and RoPC, I zap myself and request
the form of a gelatinous cube. Instead, "I feel like a new man!" Huhh?
Query 2: what happened? Both items were uncursed and I wasn't confused.

My confidence was shaken. I played it safely and zapped the last wish for
another AoLS. (in retrospect, it should have been a scroll of charging, but
I thought I would find the latter before the former.) I finish the quest 
with little problem (BTW, all those goodies scattered about on the 
Archaeologist quest went to pumping up my character even more. Namely scrolls
and spellbooks. Fort Ludios was a joke. (I used the cursed bell trick to
gain five or six levels. I got impatient after killing ten wraiths and not
getting one corpse.) Then, while going through the castle again, I get
blinded. I was so angry with myself for running into the yellow light, that
I just hit a keystroke which I think is for cure blindness. Instead, I get
the In which direction? prompt. Not thinking, I hit the "." key and get
a message like: "You feel yourself charged with energy."
	 	"You die."
Query 3: what spell was that? The most likely canidate is fireball, only
because I had no other spells above level four. The rest were really self
effect spells. (except for healing, and I KNOW that my character would be
safe from that.)

Pissed and vulnerable, I decide to play it extra safe and do some polypiling.
With five zaps, I have thirty spells, killer armor, respectable potions, and
one magic marker. (the only one I would ever find in the game. What's more,
I was polypiling a lot of tools (say fifty). I was really disappointed.) 
The pleasantest surprise was the transformation of Binky the large cat 
into a mind flayer. I went back to all the early levels and had Mr. mind
flayer pay back the shopkeepers for ignoring my business. Took down every
shopkeeper, before being killed by a purple worm. (doesn't that always 
happen?) Got a wish from a fountain and wished for (guess) AoLS.
With my confidence boosted, I prepare to go down into Gehennon when...
A disaster occurs. I stuff wands into my bag of holding when it suddenly
explodes. (minor query: are there any other wands besides cancellation which
can do this? I thought I dropped all the WoC but it was late.) I lose all my
holy water, and lots of other neat goodies (including most of my gold from
the Vault). I extort one last wish from the wand and get another blessed
bag of holding. Tasked, but hardly deterred, I tramp into Gehennon.

Hell turns out to be easy with three books of magic mapping.
Three AoLS also help  too. I polished off
Vlad and all the major demons (none even gave me the chance to pay for
passage. I guess they recognized how poor a bum I was.)
The High Priest was small game for my character too. HOWEVER, the Wizard
was one major pain. Which leads to QUERY #4 and #5:
4) How do you kill him without the ToM or VB or Mojo or FB? The blessed +6
Excalibur was doing pretty well against everything else, but it would just
hack at the wizard before he ported to the stairs. When I came close to the
up stairs, he would just climb up  a level and begin the process again.
I never realized how many levels there  were in Hell...
5) What exactly does cancelling the Wizard do?


Once I get out of Gehennon, the wizard plays it fair and no longer scoots
up the up staircase. It's a good thing too, because I had to burn one of my
three AoLS fighting him and his pets. Nothing too eventful climbing to level
1 except for an encounter with an Elven king. Feeling especially vicious,
I zap him with a wand of fire and watch him fry.
The bolt of fire hits the Elvenking.
He dies.
But wait.... an amulet begins to glow around his neck.
The bastard was wearing one of MY AoLS. And thus,, query #6: even if I knew
that he was wearing an AoLS, how could I have gotten it without his using
it?

The Elemental Planes were a pain. I read somewhere that scrolls of gold 
detection reveal the magic portal, but I had no such luck. Magic mapping
was similarly useless and my Orb of Detection detected nothing when 
applied (though I didn't actually wield it when I used it. Should this
matter?) This searching for the portal becomes especially odious on the
water level. I am reduced to my last AoLS because of a death by hunger.
Query#7: Are there shortcuts for finding that portal? And on the water
level, does the portal stay in one stationary spot, or does it move 
around? I would think it stays, but I could swear that it was first
at one spot, and then when I moved over that spot, it wasn't there. (and
yes, I am considering the effect of water displacement, so I am sure
I moved exactly over that spot.)

With my final AoLS, I rush for the middle altar, and it's the right one.
The amulet is sacrificed and history is made.

My final score was about 4.5 million points and the game took about 84,000
moves. I had 288 HP and 205 MP (lots of gain energy potions.) My final AC
was -17 and I had all the standard armor equipment. The interesting thing
though is that I worked the entire game with my +6 Excalibur. Never 
got a better weapon. Oh sure, my god decided to give me Ogremasher, but 
it was obviously not in the same league. I dubbed Sting and Orcrist, but
they were minor league weapons. Nothing else. NADA. Sort of surprising.
In another almost-ascension, I had loads of offensive weaponry. Still,
Excalibur did pretty well in it's solo job.

I vanquished 2775 creatures to the great  Nethackian unknown. This 
included 120 soldiers, 82 wraiths (but only 12 or 13 corpses were 
actually left behind), 59 gremlins (bastards jumped me on the Jubilex 
level), 79 ghosts (and literally 40 of them were my ghosts. *sigh* it's so
depressing to realize how many hours this game sucks up.) and the Wizard 12
times. I also killed something like  Yeenoghu, and I don't remember what it
was. (There were some points where I just hacked away without looking.)

And know that the epic story of my ascension is told, it's time for some
general tips.
A) genocide Master Lichs. With their summon and 'port attack, their armor
disintegration technique, and that Touch of Death, they are the most
dangerous type of monster in the game.
B) genocide eels. Why give yourselves ulcers worrying about them everytime
you see: "You feel something slither between your legs."
C) genocide dragons. Once you get disintegration resistance, it  sucks to
fight four or five of them as the Wizard's pets.
D) carry wands of teleportation. An extremely useful technique on levels
where you can't teleport is to teleport the enemy. It helps thin the ranks
considerably.
E) get that ring of polymorph control. It's invaluable in avoiding those
ripped +7 Hawaiin (spelling error, but it's late.) shirts.
F) get a stethoscope. Polypile if necessary (I did).
G) always wear an AoLS. Burn wishes if you have to. It really is amazing
how many ways this game can kill you.

Anyway, that's it for me. I'm just going to kick back and enojy this summer.
You know, spend it outside sunning on the beach and not in this dark, non-
air-conditioned room. Out of the dungeons of Nethacking, and into the bright
sunny reality.
Golly. My first ever ascension. One and a half years and (approximately)
500 games.
Couldn't have done  it without this Newsgroup. Thanks guys and Happy
Hacking!

